/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:104:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:105:Fill the parallelogram-shaped region between parallel anti-diagonal line segments with red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:106:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:107:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:108:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:109:- One non-bg color forms short diagonal segments, each lying on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = const).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:110:- Segments come in parallel pairs bounding a region to be filled.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:111:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:112:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:113:- For each main-diagonal axis (r−c = const), collect anti-diagonal segments whose span covers that axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:114:- Sort those segments by their anti-diagonal index (r+c).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:115:- Fill all bg cells lying strictly between consecutive segment pairs along that axis with red (color 2).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:116:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:117:Key insight: The two diagonal directions decouple — segments sit on anti-diagonals, and filling sweeps along main diagonals between them, forming parallelogram regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:118:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:119:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:120:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:121:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="eval" puzzle_id="58490d8a" lines="9-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:122:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:123:Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:124:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:125:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:126:- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:127:- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:128:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:129:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:130:- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:131:- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:132:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:133:Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:134:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:135:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:136:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:137:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="eval" puzzle_id="b9e38dc0" lines="7-18">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:138:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:139:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:140:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:141:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:142:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:143:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:144:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:145:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:146:- Obstacles cast "shadows" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:147:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:148:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:149:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:150:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:151:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:152:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="7ed72f31" lines="8-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:153:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:154:Mirror colored sprites using red (2) markers as reflection axes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:156:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:157:- bg = most common color. Red (2) = marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:158:- Colored sprites appear near red markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:159:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:160:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:161:- Red line within a sprite (vertical or horizontal) → mirror payload across that axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:162:- Single red pixel in a mixed sprite → point-reflect payload around it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:163:- Isolated red pixel (alone, no payload) → point-reflect each adjacent 8-connected color component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:164:- Originals remain; mirrored pixels overlay.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:165:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:166:Key insight: Red marker geometry (line vs single pixel) determines reflection type; isolated vs embedded red determines what gets reflected.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:167:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:168:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:170:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="291dc1e1" lines="7-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:171:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:172:Reorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:173:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:174:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:175:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:176:- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:177:- "Blue" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is "red."
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:178:- Solid rectangles in the interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:179:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:180:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:181:- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:182:- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:183:- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:185:Key insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:186:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:187:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:188:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:189:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="b99e7126" lines="34-48">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:190:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:191:Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:192:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:193:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:194:- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:195:- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:196:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:197:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:198:- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:199:- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:200:- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:201:- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:203:Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:204:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:205:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:206:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:207:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="80a900e0" lines="69-82">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:208:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:209:Extend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:211:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:212:- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:213:- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:214:- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:215:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:216:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:217:- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:218:- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:219:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:220:Key insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:221:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:222:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:224:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="a25697e4" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:225:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:226:Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:227:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:228:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:229:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:230:- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:231:- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:232:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:233:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:234:- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:235:- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:236:- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:237:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:238:Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:239:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:240:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:241:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:242:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="b0039139" lines="29-44">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:243:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:244:Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:245:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:246:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:247:- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:248:- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:249:- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:250:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:251:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:252:- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:253:- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:254:- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:255:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:256:Key insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:257:is inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:258:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:259:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:260:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:261:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="e3721c99" lines="69-83">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:262:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:263:Recolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:264:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:265:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:266:- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:267:- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:268:  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:269:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:270:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:271:- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:272:- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:273:- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:274:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:275:Key insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:276:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:277:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:278:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:279:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="581f7754" lines="8-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:280:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:281:Slide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:283:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:284:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:285:- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color "marker" pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:286:- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:287:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:288:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:289:- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:290:- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:291:- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:292:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:293:Key insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:294:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:295:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/prompt.md:296:
