/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:345:Move the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:346:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:347:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:348:- The background is the most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:349:- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:350:- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:351:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:352:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:353:- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:354:- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:355:- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:356:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:357:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:358:- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/3.md:359:</description>
