/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:47:Paint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:48:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:49:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:50:- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:51:- A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:52:- Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:53:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:54:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:55:- Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:56:- Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:57:- Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:58:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:59:Key insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/5.md:60:</description>
