/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:135:Predict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:136:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:137:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:138:- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:139:- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:140:- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:141:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:142:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:143:- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:144:- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:145:- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:146:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:147:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:148:- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:149:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:150:<annotation>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:151:{
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:152:  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
