/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:287:Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:288:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:289:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:290:- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:291:- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:292:- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:293:- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:294:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:295:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:296:- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:297:- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:298:- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:299:- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:300:- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:301:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:302:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:303:- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:304:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:305:<annotation>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:306:{
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:307:  "type": "transform_in_place",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:308:  "src": "monochrome regions with T-shaped color-1 control markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:309:  "transform": "recolor the region pointed to by each T stem using the original color from the two diagonal source cells behind the stem; colored-center T markers use the center color instead; erase marker cells into the source-side region",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:310:  "grid_shape": "same, except rotate 90 degrees when indicated by the colored-center control orientation",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:311:  "notes": "small non-rectangular colored scraps are absorbed into the neighboring region"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:312:}
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed454434671/2/codegen_prompts/1.md:313:</annotation>
